UID:1-8883@antir.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T140000
DTSTAMP:20260608T234116Z
URL:https://antir.org/events/lions-war-4/
SUMMARY:Lions War
DESCRIPTION:This is a Level 1: Other (Branch primary events of regional or 
 Kingdom interest) event.\n\n\nPlanned events start on Friday July 31st and
  run through Monday August 3rd.\n\n\nHot sunny days and cool crisp evening
 s await participants and revelers alike at this year's Lions War! The Baro
 ny of Lions Gate welcomes all from near and far to join in activities with
  your friends and chosen family! Return with us to the home of mighty batt
 les of the past\, and then join them in camaraderie and revels afterwards.
  Hear the clash of armoured combat upon the dusty plains of Clinton. Witne
 ss the swashbuckling elegance of rapier combat in the tavern! Hear the son
 gs of the bards as we gather around the hearths at night\, and revel in th
 e craft of the most skilled of artists! And let us not forget to mention 
 the Lions Gate Combat Archery Tournament!\n\n\nLions War has a long tradit
 ion of inviting volunteers to participate in site preparation the week pri
 or to the main event. Starting July 25th the gate will be open at 2 pm for
  registration and the site fee will cover your entire stay until the end o
 f the event. The expectation is that during this "Work Week" each person c
 ommits 1 hour per day cumulatively towards site preparation. Work meetings
  are at 9am every morning!\n\n\nMerchants are welcome to set up and displa
 y their wares along the designated merchant roads - no fee! Please contact
  the event steward to arrange for space.\n\n\nRV parking is available but 
 please be aware that generators are forbidden between the hours of 9pm and
  9am.\nDirections from the south - Follow the Trans Canada Hwy. (Hwy. 1) t
 o Cache Creek\, head north on Hwy. 97 to Clinton. Pass through town and tu
 rn left on MacDonald (right if you are taking Hwy. 97 south). Follow it up
 hill until it forks and take the right hand fork which turns into a gravel
  road that continues to head up hill. Follow it until you cross the railwa
 y tracks\, then cross a cattle guard and immediately turn left onto a road
  that parallels the railway. [Don’t mistakenly turn right at this fork 
 – it dead ends at a water tower] Follow this road and take no forks. Hon
 k as you round the blind corner and listen for others honking and go slow!
  It will eventually pass a reservoir on your left and bring you to a gate.
  Pass through the gate (open it first\, close it afterwards) and follow th
 e road to the site.\n\n\n It's time for war! Join us as the Barony of Lio
 ns Gate once again fights everyone else!\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n\n
CATEGORIES:Lions Gate
LOCATION:Clinton Creek Ranch\, 7701 Clinton Station Road\, Clinton\, BC\, C
 anada
GEO:51.089604;-121.590819
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=7701 Clinton Station Road\,
  Clinton\, BC\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Clinton Creek Ranch:geo:
 51.089604,-121.590819
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1-8959@antir.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T190000
DTSTAMP:20260616T182705Z
URL:https://antir.org/events/august-in-the-park-viking-bog-games/
SUMMARY:August in the Park &amp\; Viking Bog Games
DESCRIPTION:\n 	Join us at Daubenspeck Park...a beautiful\, shady spot...fo
 r games\, classes and contests with a viking theme! Board games\, lawn gam
 es &amp\; physical contests\, and a Holmgång contest for the fighters.\n\
 nThere will be games and contests throughout the day\, including: Hunkerha
 usen\, Glima (shield wrestling)\, Togahonk\, Jomswikinger\, and the Portho
 le Rat Toss! For the heavy fighters there will be a Holmgång contest. If 
 you're looking for something a little more relaxed\, we will have a select
 ion of board and lawn games like Hnefatafl\, Taflkast\, Kubb and Petanque.
  We'll also have some A&amp\;S classes to keep you busy.\n\nThere will be 
 plenty of activities to choose from if you wish\, or just relax in the sha
 de of the big trees and be a spectator if that’s your preference! (Be su
 re to bring a blanket or chair to sit on).\n\nThere will be a potluck in t
 he afternoon\, so bring your favorite dish\, &amp\; your feast gear. This 
 is "picnic style"\, with no electricity for crockpots.\n\nDefender's Tourn
 ey:\n\nThis year\, the trials are open to others not from the Shire! If yo
 u are open to supporting fighting activities in the Shire for the next yea
 r\, and willing to help organize next years trials\, you are welcome to vi
 e for the honour of becoming the next Shield of Hauksgardr! The lists form
 at will be determined based on the number of fighters who attend. We will 
 be fighting Holmgang tournament and the victor will be chosen based on the
  outcome of the tournament\, and participation in the Bog Olympics!\n\nTen
 tative schedule:\n\nsite open at 11:00 - No site fee!\n\nDefender's Tourne
 y 11:30\n\nGames starting at 12:30\n\nImpromptu A&amp\;S throughout the da
 y\n\ndinner prep 4:30\n\ndinner 5:00\n\nOff site by 7pm
CATEGORIES:Hauksgarðr
LOCATION:Daubenshpeck Park\, 408-412 Humbolt Street\, Bingen\, WA\, 98672\,
  RIVERS\, United States
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=408-412 Humbolt Street\, Bi
 ngen\, WA\, 98672\, RIVERS\, United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Daub
 enshpeck Park:geo:0,0
END:VEVENT
