URL:https://antir.org/events/acorn-war-xxxii/
SUMMARY:Acorn War XXXII
DESCRIPTION:This is a Level 1: Other (Branch primary events of regional or 
 Kingdom interest) event.\n\n4:00 PM August 28 to 1:00 PM August 30\, 2026\
 n\nACORN WAR XXXII SHIRE OF MOUNTAIN EDGE\nAugust 28-30\, 2026\n\nJoin us 
 for the 32nd annual Acorn War August 28-30\, 2026\, to be held at the Powe
 rland Heritage Park in Salem\, OR.  We’ll have war scenarios and rapier
  dueling. Compete for the honor of becoming a Defender in archery\, thrown
  weapons\, scribal\, art &amp\; science tournaments! MORE war scenarios th
 an you can shake a spear at: village burning\, bridge battles\, and mixed 
 archery and war combat. Activities for all ages. Saturday night bardic gat
 hering. A variety of merchants will be present. You are strongly encourage
 d to bring drinking water. Fire season will be upon us\, details to come. 
 We welcome you to volunteer in at least one area or more\, it takes a vill
 age. If there is something you want to lead\, please let event steward kno
 w.\n\nEvent Stewards: HL Asny Brunsdottir\, email: asny.brunsdottir@gmail.
 com or facebook messaging (same name). (Asny/Heidi R at 971-241-9868). Co-
 event steward is: Lady Elovel of Avalon and Archery Marshall . \n\nFees: 
 Pre-Reg (check only) will be accepted between July 20-Aug 20\, (extra $5 d
 iscount for event fee). Event Fee (camping or day trip): Adults - 35\, wit
 h $10 discount for members. Youth and children\, no charge\, waivers do ap
 ply for nonmember minors/adults. Please list on form. NO MERCHANT FEES - m
 erchants must pre-register! (Individual site fee still applies). Make chec
 ks payable to “Shire of Mountain Edge\, SCA Inc.              \n\
 nNote:  Mountain Edge Defenders and Royals are comp'd for entry fee to ev
 ent. Please let us know if you can come.  *Checks and Cash only at the si
 te\n\nSite opens at 4pm on Friday (3pm for merchants)\, and closes at 1pm 
 on Sunday.\n\nSite:  Powerland Heritage Park\, 3995 Brooklake Rd\, NE Sal
 em\, OR 97303\n\nDirections: Powerland Heritage Park is located off of I-5
 \, exit 263.\nIf coming south\, take I-5 exit 263 and turn right.\nIf comi
 ng north\, take I-5 exit 263 and turn left.\n\nDrive to the back area\, pa
 st the museum structures\, look for fields. \nPowerland Heritage Park with
  be 1/4th a mile on the right.
CATEGORIES:Mountain Edge
LOCATION:Powerland Heritage Park\, 3995 Brooklake Rd NE\, Salem\, OR\, 9730
 3\, United States
